# Lecturer Moodle Onboarding Guide

## 1. Purpose

This guide provides a structured approach for onboarding lecturers to Moodle and helping them use the Learning Management System effectively in teaching, learning and assessment.

## 2. Lecturer Onboarding Checklist

### A. Account Access
- Confirm that the lecturer has an active Moodle account.
- Verify the lecturer's login credentials.
- Confirm access to the relevant course.
- Explain how to reset a forgotten password.
- Demonstrate how to update the user profile.

### B. Course Navigation
- Demonstrate how to access the lecturer dashboard.
- Explain the course homepage layout.
- Show how to switch editing mode on and off.
- Explain how to navigate course sections and activities.

### C. Course Content Management
- Demonstrate how to upload lecture notes and presentations.
- Explain how to add files, folders and web links.
- Demonstrate how to create and organize course sections.
- Explain how to edit, hide and display learning resources.
- Encourage consistent naming of learning materials.

### D. Learning Activities
- Demonstrate how to create Moodle assignments.
- Explain assignment submission settings.
- Demonstrate how to create discussion forums.
- Explain how to configure quizzes.
- Demonstrate how to provide feedback to students.

### E. Student Management
- Demonstrate how to view enrolled students.
- Explain how to monitor student participation.
- Show how to access course activity reports.
- Explain how to communicate with students through Moodle.

### F. Assessment and Grading
- Demonstrate how to access the gradebook.
- Explain how to grade assignments.
- Demonstrate how to review quiz attempts.
- Explain how to provide feedback.
- Emphasize the importance of checking assessment settings before students begin an assessment.

## 3. Post-Onboarding Quality Checks

Before a course goes live, verify that:

- All intended learning materials are available.
- Course sections are clearly organized.
- Activities and assessment instructions are accurate.
- Quiz availability and timing settings are correct.
- Assignment submission settings are appropriate.
- Student access has been checked.
- Course content is accessible and easy to navigate.

## 4. Lecturer Support and Follow-Up

After onboarding:

1. Provide a channel for reporting Moodle issues.
2. Record support requests and their resolution.
3. Identify recurring training needs.
4. Schedule follow-up support where necessary.
5. Collect lecturer feedback to improve future onboarding.

## 5. Common Support Issues

| Issue | Recommended support action |
|---|---|
| Lecturer cannot log in | Verify account status and assist with password recovery. |
| Course is not visible | Check enrolment and course availability. |
| Cannot upload files | Check file size, file type and course permissions. |
| Quiz settings are incorrect | Review quiz configuration with the lecturer. |
| Students cannot access activities | Check availability restrictions and access conditions. |
| Grades are missing | Review gradebook setup and assessment configuration. |

## 6. Expected Outcomes

Successful onboarding should enable lecturers to:

- Navigate Moodle confidently.
- Manage course content independently.
- Create and manage learning activities.
- Configure online assessments appropriately.
- Monitor student participation and performance.
- Access technical support when required.

